The fix for crbug 565681452 ("[ServiceWorker] Invoke fetch response callbacks directly
from Take()"): chromium/src main commit 40ec50192c4b3776df207c373cfcc025a168e92b
(main@{#1745288}, Change-Id I565681452b767bc1b1da17c51457dc471a0727d7), merged to the 159
branch as 3912f18323. Its 158 merge (Gerrit 8835040) is pending, as of 8127@{#1921}.

ServiceWorkerGlobalScope::RespondToFetchEventWithNoResponse() removed the response callback
from fetch_response_callbacks_ before recording the event in
pending_streaming_upload_fetch_events_, and kept an intermediate raw pointer to the
returned wrapper. The fix records the event first and calls OnFallback() directly on the
returned wrapper; the sibling RespondTo*() methods get the same inline
Take()->Value()->On*() pattern.

This is the main commit's change without its test (service_worker_global_scope_test.cc),
regenerated against 158's file (the same at the .66 tag and at #1921; the main commit's
hunks apply to it at offsets only, with no fuzz). The result is byte-identical to the file
of the pending 158 merge's current patchset (3). Drop this once 158 gets the fix (check
that the merged change is the same).

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/service_worker/service_worker_global_scope.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/service_worker/service_worker_global_scope.cc
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/service_worker/service_worker_global_scope.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/service_worker/service_worker_global_scope.cc
@@ -994,8 +994,6 @@
   // out.
   if (!fetch_response_callbacks_.Contains(fetch_event_id))
     return;
-  mojom::blink::ServiceWorkerFetchResponseCallback* response_callback =
-      fetch_response_callbacks_.Take(fetch_event_id)->Value().get();
 
   auto timing = mojom::blink::ServiceWorkerFetchEventTiming::New();
   timing->dispatch_event_time = event_dispatch_time;
@@ -1007,8 +1005,14 @@
     pending_streaming_upload_fetch_events_.insert(fetch_event_id, fetch_event);
   }
 
-  response_callback->OnFallback(std::move(request_body), std::move(timing),
-                                std::move(errors));
+  // Take and invoke the callback after all Oilpan allocations (such as
+  // `pending_streaming_upload_fetch_events_.insert()`), as a GC triggered
+  // after `Take()` would collect the unrooted `HeapMojoRemote` wrapper and
+  // reset its underlying Mojo proxy before `OnFallback()` is called.
+  fetch_response_callbacks_.Take(fetch_event_id)
+      ->Value()
+      ->OnFallback(std::move(request_body), std::move(timing),
+                   std::move(errors));
 }
